BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What Does It Mean to Be American? with Chisao Hata
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T193000
UID:699f4180403a4e5652dd72e4@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This conversation explores what it means to be “American\,
 ” examining identity\, belonging\, and inclusion through discussion and 
 nonverbal activities. Participants will share personal and community persp
 ectives on who is included in “We the People.”
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f4180403a4e5652dd72e4
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CivicUs: What Does It Mean to Be a Citizen? with Prakash Chenjeri
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T133000
UID:699f40bbd34a4e759286f315@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In the United States\, most people would say they believe in d
 emocracy. But do we all understand the word in the same way? Where does th
 e concept of democracy come from\, and what makes “the rule of the peopl
 e” work? This conversation will dig into the history\, philosophy\, and 
 practical workings of democracy. We’ll look at the words of important po
 litical thinkers from the past\, the US Constitution\, and research on cha
 llenges to democracy in the present day. We’ll leave with a better sense
  of what we mean when we say democracy and how to participate in the democ
 ratic process locally and nationally.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Shute Park
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f40bbd34a4e759286f315
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Understanding and Managing Your Digital Legacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260518T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260518T173000
UID:699f3ecbec71a31f5b4131d4@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In an increasingly digital world\, few people think about what
  will happen to their email\, social media\, or personal accounts after th
 ey pass. Learn what steps you can take to manage your digital legacy or le
 arn how to manage the digital legacy of a loved one. This is not a course 
 on estate planning or legal advice.\nRegistration required.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Brookwood
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f3ecbec71a31f5b4131d4
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
