BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:When History Repeats Itself: A Japanese American Family’s Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T130000
UID:699f4dc25506be0745fefaf3@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join a local Japanese American community member as she shares 
 her family’s experience during World War II\, when her father and uncles
  were removed from their Portland high school and incarcerated at the Port
 land Livestock Exhibition Center before being sent to Minidoka\, Idaho. Th
 rough personal storytelling and historical context\, the talk reflects on 
 wartime incarceration and how fear and suspicion of immigrants continue to
  echo today. Bring your lunch!
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Shute Park
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f4dc25506be0745fefaf3
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Outdoor Adventure Apps
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T143000
UID:698fa9f4b48451fc3c02a1f4@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that your smartphone can enhance your outdoor exp
 eriences? This lecture introduces popular outdoor apps for all kinds of wi
 lderness adventures from hiking and biking to camping and fishing. You'll 
 learn about useful app features such as GPS navigation\, nature ID\, real-
 time updates\, and more. We'll also cover considerations for choosing apps
  and best practices regarding data and privacy.\nPresented by Meals on Whe
 els People. While all are welcome at this lecture\, the curriculum is desi
 gned for adults ages 55+.\nRegistration is required.
LOCATION:Cedar Mill Library\, Elm & Oak Room
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698fa9f4b48451fc3c02a1f4
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
