BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poetry Open Mic [at Bethany Library Annex]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T193000
UID:69decd0524bd39b0b5e768df@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you been looking for a way to share your poetry? Do you e
 njoy \nhearing what others in your community are passionate about? If so\,
  join \nus for a poetry open mic night where you can share original work o
 r read\n your favorite poem.\nGeneral Guidelines:\nReading Room will open 
 at 6:00 p.m.\nReaders must sign in by 6:10 p.m.\nPoetry readings will begi
 n by 6:15 p.m.\nOrder of readings will follow sign-in sheet\nAllowed time 
 will depend on number of readers signed up\nObserver feedback / comments w
 ill open after the final poet has read\nGuidelines for Readers:\nPoems sho
 uld not contain language unsuitable for family\, e.g. profanity\, sexually
  explicit\nTime limitations will be strictly enforced to ensure all reader
 s can participate\nAs a courtesy\, please remain present until the final p
 oems are read
LOCATION:Bethany Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69decd0524bd39b0b5e768df
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Navigator One on One Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T120000
UID:68f17e4861706d28001e190f@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Digital Navigator One-On-One Tech Help each Wednesday from 10:
 00 a.m. -12:00 p.m. in the library. Need help with digital questions or jo
 b searches? This free program is in partnership with American Connection C
 orps & The Washington County Cooperative Library Services. Call the librar
 y at 503 324-1382 to schedule a session.\nIf no appointments are scheduled
  drop in tech help will be available.\nThe Digital Navigator Program (DNP)
  is a free service made possible by a partnership\nbetween Washington Coun
 ty Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) and the Washington\nCounty Broadba
 nd Action Team. The DNP is funded in part by American Connections\nCorps\,
  an AmeriCorps program dedicated to advancing economic prosperity by bridg
 ing\nthe digital divide. This project is being supported\, in part\, by fe
 deral award number\nSLFRP0228 awarded to Washington County by the U.S. Dep
 artment of the Treasury.
LOCATION:Banks Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/68f17e4861706d28001e190f
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
